,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**No.** Exchange volume reflects only secondary-market trading, not total accessible liquidity.\n\n**Creation/redemption:** Authorized participants (APs) can create ETF shares by delivering the underlying basket (or cash) to the issuer, or redeem shares for the basket. This arbitrage keeps prices near NAV and lets supply adjust to demand. An ETF's liquidity therefore depends largely on its **underlying holdings**, not just its own trading history.\n\n**Other indicators:**\n- Bid-ask spread (quoted and effective) through the day\n- Displayed depth/quote size at the NBBO\n- Premium/discount to NAV/iNAV and its volatility\n- Underlying securities' volume, spreads and market hours (e.g., foreign or bond markets)\n- Creation unit size, fees and cash vs. in-kind terms\n- Number of active APs and market makers\n- Market conditions and volatility\n\nFor large orders, consider consulting a liquidity provider or block desk. None of this guarantees execution at a given size or price.","ttft_ms":1292,"type":"result","duration_ms":3779,"uuid":"a1da73f5-1825-4430-86e1-4a4c5fa97c41","ttft_stream_ms":1071,"time_to_request_ms":66,"first_content_frame_ms":1072,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
